								Wicked Warder<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=418"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1221.msg12168#msg12168"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1221.msg12168#msg12168">Re: Shattered Emerald of Corruption Business</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #5 on:</b> October 28, 2004, 05:23:25 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I am a lvl 66 ranger and yeah it is a sucky camp. Hey if you are fidning people willing to drop 40k on the stone, go you. As long as you are not creating the bottleneck for people who do want to camp it on there own.&nbsp; Which you said if people want to then go for it. So go you 
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
